      description: "Ennumo (pegfilgrastim-pccg) is a long-acting, pegylated G-CSF biosimilar that binds the G-CSF receptor and expands neutrophil precursors to support recovery after chemotherapy or marrow-damaging radiation. FDA approved on May 7, 2026 and biosimilar to Neulasta, it still has product-specific presentation and H-ARS dosing boundaries, so an order cannot be inferred from the word pegfilgrastim alone. In H-ARS it is started as soon as possible after a suspected or confirmed myelosuppressive dose greater than 2 Gy because marrow progenitors are injured before the blood-count nadir becomes visible. It supports neutrophil recovery but does not remove radionuclides, replace antimicrobial care, or repair gastrointestinal, skin, neurovascular, or pulmonary radiation injury.",
