      administrationTiming: ["For credible H-ARS, begin as soon as possible after suspected or confirmed exposure above 2 Gy; do not wait for neutropenia to become profound because the biologic injury precedes the CBC nadir.", "For adults of any weight and pediatric patients weighing at least 45 kg, the H-ARS label uses two 6 mg subcutaneous doses one week apart.", "Do not administer ENNUMO for H-ARS to a pediatric patient below 45 kg: no ENNUMO presentation permits accurate weight-based dosing below that boundary. Select a different label-supported countermeasure through the radiation-emergency protocol rather than improvising a partial syringe dose."],
