      description: "Filkri (filgrastim-laha) is a short-acting G-CSF biosimilar that binds the G-CSF receptor and expands neutrophil precursors to reduce the depth and duration of neutropenia. Because nonpegylated filgrastim clears faster than pegfilgrastim, H-ARS treatment uses daily weight-based dosing until the label-defined ANC recovery endpoint rather than two separated doses. FDA approved on January 15, 2026 and biosimilar to Neupogen, Filkri is supplied only in 300 microgram/0.5 mL and 480 microgram/0.8 mL prefilled syringes, not a vial. Because product-specific presentation and dosing differ, a search for Filkri must not open the generic class card or silently substitute another suffix. Therapy begins as soon as possible after a suspected or confirmed myelosuppressive exposure greater than 2 Gy. A baseline CBC helps define injury, but lack of immediate laboratory access should not delay treatment after a credible exposure.",
