      usedToTreat: "Recognition and coordinated treatment of hematopoietic acute radiation syndrome after a myelosuppressive whole-body or substantial partial-body exposure. The pathway links current G-CSF, GM-CSF, and thrombopoietin-receptor products to supportive care without confusing marrow injury with internal contamination or other radiation syndromes.",
      description: "H-ARS countermeasures are marrow-directed biologic therapies that stimulate neutrophil or platelet recovery after ionizing radiation kills hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells, which otherwise produces a delayed fall in lymphocytes, neutrophils, platelets, and red cells after a potentially deceptive early period. FDA-listed countermeasures now include product-specific filgrastim and pegfilgrastim products, sargramostim, and romiplostim; the 2025-2026 additions include Releuko, Fylnetra, Armlupeg, Filkri, and Ennumo. Choice depends on the exact label, availability, weight, lineage problem, and incident protocol. No growth factor substitutes for serial blood counts, infection and bleeding management, transfusion support, biodosimetry, and care of gastrointestinal, cutaneous, pulmonary, or neurovascular injury.",
      mechanism: "Ionizing radiation kills rapidly dividing marrow progenitors and damages the stem-cell niche, so circulating counts fall only after mature cells complete their normal lifespan. G-CSF products such as filgrastim and pegfilgrastim expand neutrophil precursors; sargramostim activates broader myeloid recovery through GM-CSF signaling; romiplostim stimulates the thrombopoietin receptor and megakaryocyte production. These mechanisms explain why the products are complementary rather than interchangeable. Potassium iodide blocks thyroid radioiodine uptake, Prussian blue binds cesium or thallium, and DTPA chelates selected transuranics; none of those actions repairs marrow progenitors.",
      administrationTiming: ["Activate radiation-emergency, public-health, hematology, and incident-command pathways immediately; estimate dose from event data, time to vomiting, serial absolute lymphocyte counts, and biodosimetry without delaying indicated treatment.", "Start the selected exact FDA-labeled H-ARS product as soon as possible, then follow its weight, presentation, interval, and recovery endpoint rather than treating all biosimilars as interchangeable.", "Continue CBC, infection, bleeding, mucosal, fluid, electrolyte, and multi-organ surveillance through nadir and recovery because apparent early stability does not exclude lethal injury."],
